 - [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL include the active snapshot date in the result.
 - [ ] **REG-003**: When a snapshot has an invalid signature, an unsupported schema version, or duplicate serial numbers, the system SHALL reject the import and retain the active snapshot.
 - [ ] **REG-004**: When a valid replacement snapshot is activated, the system SHALL expose all of its records together without exposing a partially imported snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-005**: When a valid snapshot is imported, the system SHALL build a SQLite index from its records and atomically swap it as the active index.
+- [ ] **REG-006**: When the SQLite index is built, the system SHALL store serial number as primary key, calibration date, due date, description, and the snapshot date as a global property.
+- [ ] **REG-007**: When a lookup executes, the system SHALL complete the point query within 250 ms on a kiosk with 4 GB of RAM for up to 90,000 records.
+- [ ] **REG-008**: If the SQLite index file is missing or corrupt at startup, the system SHALL report a clear error and remain in a state awaiting a valid snapshot import.
